{"id":1,"name":"الفاتحة","transliteration":"Al-Faatiha","translation":"The Opening","type":"meccan","totalVerses":7,"verses":[{"id":1,"arabic":"بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ","translation":"In the name of Allāh,[2] the Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful.[3]","footnotes":"[2]- Allāh is a proper name belonging only to the one Almighty God, Creator and Sustainer of the heavens and the earth and all that is within them, the Eternal and Absolute, to whom alone all worship is due.\n[3]- Ar-Raḥmān and ar-Raḥeem are two names of Allāh derived from the word \"raḥmah\" (mercy) . In Arabic grammar both are intensive forms of \"merciful\" (i.e., extremely merciful) . A complimentary and comprehensive meaning is intended by using both together. Raḥmān is used only to describe Allāh, while raḥeem might be used to describe a person as well. The Prophet (ﷺ) was described in the Qur’ān as raḥeem. Raḥmān is above the human level (i.e., intensely merciful) . Since one usually understands intensity to be something of short duration, Allāh describes Himself also as raḥeem (i.e., continually merciful) . Raḥmān also carries a wider meaning - merciful to all creation. Justice is a part of this mercy. Raḥeem includes the concept of speciality - especially and specifically merciful to the believers. Forgiveness is a part of this mercy. In addition, Raḥmān is adjectival, referring to an attribute of Allāh and is part of His essence. Raḥeem is verbal, indicating what He does: i.e., bestowing and implementing mercy.","words":[{"position":1,"arabic":"بِسْمِ","root":"سمو","lemma":"اسْم","role":"noun","segments":[{"arabic":"بِ","type":"P","flags":["P","PREF"],"lemma":"ب","role":"preposition","pos":"Preposition","prefix":true,"description":"Preposition","gloss":"with / by","glossSource":"qac-prefix"},{"arabic":"سْمِ","type":"N","flags":[],"root":"سمو","lemma":"اسْم","case":"GEN","gender":"M","role":"noun","pos":"Noun","prefix":false,"description":"Noun — genitive, masculine"}],"gloss":"In (the) name","translit":"bis'mi"},{"position":2,"arabic":"ٱللَّهِ","root":"أله","lemma":"اللَّه","role":"proper","segments":[{"arabic":"ٱللَّهِ","type":"N","flags":["PN"],"root":"أله","lemma":"اللَّه","case":"GEN","role":"proper","pos":"Proper noun","prefix":false,"description":"Proper noun — genitive","gloss":"Allah","glossSource":"qac-lemma"}],"gloss":"(of) Allah","translit":"l-lahi"},{"position":3,"arabic":"ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ","root":"رحم","lemma":"رَحْمٰن","role":"adjective","segments":[{"arabic":"ٱل","type":"P","flags":["DET","PREF"],"lemma":"ال","role":"determiner","pos":"Determiner (the)","prefix":true,"description":"Determiner (the)","gloss":"the","glossSource":"reviewed-table"},{"arabic":"رَّحْمَٰنِ","type":"N","flags":["ADJ"],"root":"رحم","lemma":"رَحْمٰن","case":"GEN","gender":"M","number":"S","role":"adjective","pos":"Adjective","prefix":false,"description":"Adjective — genitive, masculine, singular"}],"gloss":"the Most Gracious","translit":"l-raḥmāni"},{"position":4,"arabic":"ٱلرَّحِيمِ","root":"رحم","lemma":"رَحِيم","role":"adjective","segments":[{"arabic":"ٱل","type":"P","flags":["DET","PREF"],"lemma":"ال","role":"determiner","pos":"Determiner (the)","prefix":true,"description":"Determiner (the)","gloss":"the","glossSource":"reviewed-table"},{"arabic":"رَّحِيمِ","type":"N","flags":["ADJ"],"root":"رحم","lemma":"رَحِيم","case":"GEN","gender":"M","number":"S","role":"adjective","pos":"Adjective","prefix":false,"description":"Adjective — genitive, masculine, singular"}],"gloss":"the Most Merciful","translit":"l-raḥīmi"}],"tajweed":[[7,8,"hamzat_wasl"],[15,16,"hamzat_wasl"],[16,17,"lam_shamsiyyah"],[24,25,"madd_2"],[28,29,"hamzat_wasl"],[29,30,"lam_shamsiyyah"],[35,36,"madd_246"]]},{"id":2,"arabic":"ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ","translation":"[All] praise is [due] to Allāh, Lord[4] of the worlds -","footnotes":"[4]- When referring to Allāh (subḥānahu wa taʿālā) , the Arabic term \"rabb\" (translated as \"Lord\") includes all of the following meanings: \"owner, master, ruler, controller, sustainer, provider, guardian and caretaker.\"","words":[{"position":1,"arabic":"ٱلْحَمْدُ","root":"حمد","lemma":"حَمْد","role":"noun","segments":[{"arabic":"ٱلْ","type":"P","flags":["DET","PREF"],"lemma":"ال","role":"determiner","pos":"Determiner (the)","prefix":true,"description":"Determiner (the)","gloss":"the","glossSource":"reviewed-table"},{"arabic":"حَمْدُ","type":"N","flags":[],"root":"حمد","lemma":"حَمْد","case":"NOM","gender":"M","role":"noun","pos":"Noun","prefix":false,"description":"Noun — nominative, masculine"}],"gloss":"All praises and thanks","translit":"al-ḥamdu"},{"position":2,"arabic":"لِلَّهِ","root":"أله","lemma":"اللَّه","role":"proper","segments":[{"arabic":"لِ","type":"P","flags":["P","PREF"],"lemma":"ل","role":"preposition","pos":"Preposition","prefix":true,"description":"Preposition","gloss":"for","glossSource":"qac-prefix"},{"arabic":"لَّهِ","type":"N","flags":["PN"],"root":"أله","lemma":"اللَّه","case":"GEN","role":"proper","pos":"Proper noun","prefix":false,"description":"Proper noun — genitive","gloss":"Allah","glossSource":"qac-lemma"}],"gloss":"(be) to Allah","translit":"lillahi"},{"position":3,"arabic":"رَبِّ","root":"ربب","lemma":"رَبّ","role":"noun","segments":[{"arabic":"رَبِّ","type":"N","flags":[],"root":"ربب","lemma":"رَبّ","case":"GEN","gender":"M","role":"noun","pos":"Noun","prefix":false,"description":"Noun — genitive, masculine"}],"gloss":"the Lord","translit":"rabbi"},{"position":4,"arabic":"ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ","root":"علم","lemma":"عالَم","role":"noun","segments":[{"arabic":"ٱلْ","type":"P","flags":["DET","PREF"],"lemma":"ال","role":"determiner","pos":"Determiner (the)","prefix":true,"description":"Determiner (the)","gloss":"the","glossSource":"reviewed-table"},{"arabic":"عَٰلَمِينَ","type":"N","flags":[],"root":"علم","lemma":"عالَم","case":"GEN","gender":"M","number":"P","role":"noun","pos":"Noun","prefix":false,"description":"Noun — genitive, masculine, plural"}],"gloss":"of the un